{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"system"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemRelation","text":"MXLSystemRelation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"system","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/system","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The system-relation attribute group distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"particular part where the element appears.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/system"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV6systemAA17MXLSystemRelationOSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"system"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSystemRelation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","title":"system"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/system":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/system","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/system","abstract":[{"text":"The system-relation attribute group distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"particular part where the element appears.","type":"text"}],"title":"system","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"system"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemRelationO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLSystemRelation"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","abstract":[{"text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLEnding","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemRelation":{"title":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The system-relation type distinguishes elements that are associated with a system rather than the particular","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part where the element appears. A value of only-top indicates that the element should appear only on the top","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part of the current system. A value of also-top indicates that the element should appear on both the current","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part and the top part of the current system. If this value appears in a score, when parts are created the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element should only appear once in this part, not twice. A value of none indicates that the element is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"associated only with the current part, not with the system.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemRelation","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemRelation","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemrelation"}}}